---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Eligibility Criteria — SRM Compass"
  description="Official 2026-27 B.Tech eligibility criteria and transparent documentation of source conflicts on SRM’s portal."
>
  <section class="blk">
    <div class="w">
      <h1>Eligibility</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Official admission requirements for B.Tech programmes across SRMIST campuses for the 2026–2027 academic cycle.
      </p>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          <b>Source conflict.</b> We show SRM’s 2026-27 rule: at least 60% aggregate in Physics, Mathematics and one more qualifying subject. Biotechnology and biomedical programmes need 60% in PCM, PMB, PCB or similar combinations. 7 of these 8 rows in SRM’s fee table still carry older text that says 50% and cites SRMJEEE (UG) 2022.
        </p>
        <details>
          <summary>See both versions</summary>
          <p>
            2026-27 criteria section: 60% aggregate (3 subjects). Fee table eligibility column: 50% aggregate, 2022 wording. Both are on{' '}
            <a
              href="https://www.srmist.edu.in/admission-india/engineering/"
              rel="noopener"
              target="_blank"
            >
              the same SRM page
            </a>
            . Confirm on SRM’s page before you rely on either.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>2026–2027 Rule Breakdown</h3>
        <ol class="st">
          <li>
            <strong>Qualifying Examination:</strong> Applicant should have passed in Higher Secondary examination (10+2 pattern) or appearing in Higher Secondary examination in the current academic year with a <strong>minimum of 60% aggregate</strong> (3 subjects) in Physics (mandatory), Mathematics (mandatory) and at least one of Chemistry / Biotechnology / Biology / Computer Science / Information Technology / Informatics Practices / Engineering Graphics / Botany and Zoology.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Biotechnology &amp; Biomedical:</strong> Minimum 60% aggregate in PCM / PMB / PCB / PCB or Z (Botany or Zoology). Students who have not studied Mathematics in 10+2 must undertake an additional bridge course in Mathematics.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Nationality and Age:</strong> Resident Indian. Should have attained the age of 16 years and 6 months on the 31st July of the calendar year in which the 12th Board examination is held.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Entrance Exam:</strong> Admission is through the national-level entrance exam <strong>SRMJEEE (UG)</strong>.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn p" href="/#programmes">Compare programmes</a>
        <a class="btn s" href="/apply">How applying works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
